    "_comment": "Bake the yaw INTO the model so its centreline is a coordinate plane. Glitch's drum axle measures [0.4483, 0.0567, -0.8921] in model space \u2014 27 degrees off any axis \u2014 which means the bot's plane of symmetry is 27 degrees off too, and every tool downstream works in axis-aligned boxes and planes. Rotating every part about Y by -1.1055 rad puts the axle on model +X, so the symmetry plane becomes x=0 and the mirror below is expressible at all. modelYaw absorbs the same rotation in the other direction, so nothing about how the bot faces changes.",
